message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, together
  with the associated article listed under references.
type: software
title: Direct Field Method examples for photonics and plasmonics
version: 0.1.0
# date-released: "YYYY-MM-DD"
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/sq-modelling/direct-field-method-photonics-plasmonics"
abstract: >-
  Fortran programs and case inputs for the numerical examples of the tutorial
  "Computational photonics and plasmonics: A direct physical approach",
  including the gap-graded surface meshes of the three-rod example and the
  Python script that generates them; a Python exercise that compares a computed
  result with Mie theory; the numerical results and Python plotting scripts for
  Figs. 2, 3, 5 and 7; and a Python post-processing script that computes the
  fields and radar cross section of perfect conductors from the surface current
  of the magnetic-field solution, as used for the low-frequency case of Fig. 3.
  The Direct Field Method solves Maxwell's equations in the
  frequency domain directly for the Cartesian components of the electric and
  magnetic fields with non-singular boundary integral equations discretized by
  curved six-node quadratic triangular elements.
